{%
  set content = {
    "title": "Ship at the speed of AI",
    "eyebrow": "Agentic engineering consulting",
    "text": "With AI, frontend teams can generate more code faster than ever. That moves the bottleneck downstream to review, testing, and release. Code that never ships has no value, and shipping broken code even has negative value. Increasing velocity sustainably and outpacing the competition takes engineering infrastructure and pipelines that let teams ship consistently, with confidence, at the pace AI makes possible.",
    "image": "/assets/images/hero/agentic-engineering.jpg",
    "alt": "Desk setup for agentic engineering work",
    "loading": "eager"
  }
%}
{{ colorHero('purple', content) }}

<section class="container container--lg my-5">
  <div class="workshops-page__intro">
    <div class="workshops-page__intro-text">
      <p>
        Most frontend teams aren’t seeing the velocity gains AI makes possible. Teams using AI merge
        far more pull requests, but industry data shows bugs per pull request rising substantially,
        leading to degraded quality and rework that eats up the velocity gains. Many teams were
        already struggling to keep up with the code their engineers wrote by hand before AI, with
        review queues growing and slow builds and flaky tests getting in the way. Until they fix
        that, these teams can’t benefit from AI and keep up with their competition.
      </p>
      <p>
        Mainmatter has helped frontend teams improve their setups and ship faster for years. The
        same techniques and infrastructure that allowed Qonto to scale up its frontend team quickly
        without sacrificing quality are what teams need to turn AI-generated code into shipped
        features: fast, extensive, and reliable testing, stable delivery automation, and
        comprehensive observability. We bring that experience to modernize our clients’ software
        development lifecycle (SDLC) and build the frontend software factories of the future.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%
  set list_1 = {
    "title": "Assess the status quo",
    "text": "We map your team's setup and maturity, covering composition and experience, tooling and infrastructure, development practices, testing and release processes. That surfaces the blockers holding back your software delivery lifecycle."
  }
%}
{%
  set list_2 = {
    "title": "Define what success looks like",
    "text": "Together we set the target and put tracking in place for metrics like velocity, lead time for changes, and change failure rate, so progress stays visible and grounded in real outcomes."
  }
%}
{%
  set list_3 = {
    "title": "Clear the path",
    "text": "We close the gaps in your delivery pipeline: testing, automation, infrastructure, observability. A pipeline that strains under today's volume will only buckle when AI accelerates code production."
  }
%}
{%
  set list_4 = {
    "title": "Roll out tools and practices",
    "text": "With the foundation in place, we roll out tools incrementally, working alongside your engineers to support and mentor them as they go."
  }
%}
